  "Number": 15,
  "Question": "The arithmetic mean (average) of four numbers is \\(85.\\) If the largest of these numbers is \\(97,\\) then the mean of the remaining three numbers is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(81.0\\)",
    "B": "\\(82.7\\)",
    "C": "\\(83.0\\)",
    "D": "\\(84.0\\)",
    "E": "\\(84.3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The mean is the total divided by the number of values, so the four numbers have total\n\\[\n4\\times85=340.\n\\]\nRemoving \\(97\\) leaves a total of \\(340-97=243\\) for the remaining three numbers. Their mean is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{243}{3}=81.0.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(81.0\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
